[3] Unit-excess prime-q shadow: n=2 is exact perfection; n=14 is deficient
  apex n=2: fractions a/(n*a-1)
    a=1   q=1    prime=False prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0
    a=2   q=3    prime=True  prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0 actual_A=2
    a=4   q=7    prime=True  prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0 actual_A=2
    a=8   q=15   prime=False prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0
    a=16  q=31   prime=True  prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0 actual_A=2
    a=64  q=127  prime=True  prime-q-A=       2  2-A=       0 actual_A=2

  apex n=14: fractions a/(n*a-1)
    a=1   q=13   prime=True  prime-q-A=   14/13  2-A=   12/13 actual_A=14/13
    a=2   q=27   prime=False prime-q-A=    14/9  2-A=     4/9
    a=4   q=55   prime=False prime-q-A=   98/55  2-A=   12/55
    a=8   q=111  prime=False prime-q-A=   70/37  2-A=    4/37
    a=16  q=223  prime=True  prime-q-A= 434/223  2-A=  12/223 actual_A=434/223
    a=64  q=895  prime=False prime-q-A=1778/895  2-A=  12/895

  Identity: for a=2^k and prime q=n*a-1,
    sigma(a*q)/(a*q) = n(2a-1)/(na-1) = 2 + (2-n)/(na-1).
  Therefore exact perfection is forced by n=2; LRC14 has defect 12/(14a-1).

[4] Kuratowski/Wagner guardrails for the product ledger
  K5 edges = 10, but Farey term 2/5 gives K_{2,5} with 10 edges and it is planar.
  K3,3 edges = 9, but 3/3 is not a reduced Farey term; 1/9 is a star.
  The first reduced Farey complete-bipartite term containing K3,3 is 3/4 -> K_{3,4}.
  K5 disjoint-union K3,3 has (edges,vertices)=(19,11), the unreduced density
  mixture of (10,5) and (9,6), but it is nonplanar only because it already
  contains the two irreducible obstruction cores.  Minors/subdivisions compose;
  mediants and edge-density averages do not manufacture new forbidden minors.

[5] Tournament Analysis over carrier roles
  Alternate vertex sets considered:
    Farey fractions, products, graph isomorphism types, minor cores,
    factor pairs, divisor atoms, density ratios, wall crossings, and proof obligations.
  Chosen vertices are carrier roles.  The quotient preserves proof-role pressure
  and destroys exact runner geometry and exact graph embeddings.
  Pairwise observable: earlier role in each criterion beats later role.
  Gauge: majority of five criteria; tie Hamiltonian path:
    minor_closure > kuratowski_core > K33_incidence > perfect_abundancy > unit_excess_chain > farey_level > product_edges > raw_edge_density
  Score histogram: {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 5: 2, 6: 2}
  Scores:
